index 0000000..10bf1d0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/LATE-HUDLESS-D3D11.md
@@ -0,0 +1,79 @@
+# Explicit late HUDless input for Last Epoch
+
+This is a local GPL-3.0 modification of Skynizz/optiscaler-dlss5 v1.2.1,
+commit `6bfc4389c25054ef6747df6e6b1b470e9541c4da`. The source archive SHA256 is
+`1EAAD2223E679A935426E922F86A0341232AE96641579FEC4A5B34004A1CD507`.
+The original archive remains in `../../downloads/optiscaler-source-1.2.1.zip`.
+Keep this source, its GPL license and the original third-party notices with any
+distribution of the modified backend. This variant has not been validated in-game.
+
+## Why the extra submission exists
+
+DLSS SR must run before bloom/color grading, but DLSSG needs display-ready scene
+color after those effects and before the UI is drawn. The upstream heuristic can
+latch the first SR output; submitting that image as HUDless misidentifies later
+postprocessing changes as UI. This extension requires an explicit late callback
+and leaves the heuristic disabled.
+
+## ABI version 1
+
+Resolve the three exported names from the locally built backend using
+`GetProcAddress`; the unmodified backend does not export them. Function pointer
+types and result codes are in `OptiScaler/hudfix/ExternalHudless_Dx11.h`.
+
+1. Check `OptiScaler_GetHudlessD3D11Version() == 1`.
+2. On the immediate render thread, immediately after a successful NGX SR
+   evaluation, call `OptiScaler_GetHudlessFrameTokenD3D11()`. Store its nonzero
+   token with the same camera/frame's bridge state. Zero means unavailable.
+3. Later on that render thread, after final bloom/grading/output transform and
+   before UI, call `OptiScaler_SubmitHudlessD3D11(context, texture, token)` once.
+   Retain the COM texture until the callback executes. The function records a
+   copy immediately, so the source can be released after that callback returns.
+4. Require return value 1 before reporting successful HUDless submission.
+   Stale, already-presented and duplicate frames are rejected. Do not submit a
+   previous camera/frame's token or call NGX Evaluate a second time.
+
+The texture must be single-sampled, one array slice, exactly swapchain-sized and
+in the same orientation and numeric color encoding as the final presented scene.
+API1 accepts only SDR 8-bit RGBA/BGRA UNORM/SRGB swapchains and source textures
+from those format families (including typeless source members used by Unity).
+HDR, 10-bit and float swapchains or inputs return `InvalidTexture` (-4). The
+caller must additionally disable this path when Unity HDR output is active;
+an 8-bit storage format alone does not establish the presentation transfer function.
+The existing format transfer handles a compatible color storage-format change;
+it does not supply tone mapping, gamma conversion, resizing or vertical flipping.
+The bridge must capture the actual final scene, not merely a pre-UI image from an
+earlier stage. Output must differ from the presented backbuffer only by UI.
+
+## Configuration and synchronization
+
+Use `FrameGen.FGInput=Upscaler`, `FrameGen.DisableHudless=false`,
+`OptiFG.HUDFix=false`, and `FSRFG.UseMutexForSwapchain=true` (the default).
+Keep FG disabled until its ordinary depth/motion/color path is validated.
+The explicit API intentionally refuses to coexist with heuristic HUDless capture.
+
+The current FG frame token is captured without starting another frame. Submission
+locks the existing presentation mutex, validates the frame, copies the final
+D3D11 texture into the existing capture ring, shares it with D3D12, calls the
+existing D3D11-to-D3D12 fence synchronization, and tags the exact matching FG
+resource slot. It uses `ValidNow` tagging, allowing Streamline to make its
+required copy. Tokens are invalidated on upstream reset and resource-release
+paths. These safeguards still require runtime resize/Alt-Tab/shutdown testing.
+
+## Build and validation
+
+Run `Build-Local.ps1` from this source tree. It uses installed VS2022 v143 and the
+Windows SDK, and disables upstream packaging build events. The output is isolated
+in `local-build`; the script never copies it to `stage` or a game directory.
+The fork README documents v145, so v143 compatibility must be established by the
+build result. The supplied precompiled shaders and libraries are reused.
+The local v143 build uses embedded compile symbols (`/Z7`) and the 64-bit host
+compiler to avoid the shared PDB manager failure in this environment. Compiler
+parallelism is bounded by `-ParallelProcesses` (default 4). The local source also
+suppresses the upstream frame-gap warning when FG is disabled/inactive; frame
+and resource-ring bookkeeping is unchanged.
+
+Before deploying, verify all three exports, then validate SR/FG with HUDless off.
+After connecting the late callback, compare the tagged HUDless image to the final
+backbuffer with UI hidden; bloom, grading and scene pixels should match. Exercise
+combat, map changes, resize, Alt-Tab, disabled FG and stale/duplicate callbacks.
